The Tragedy of the Divisible Prince.

Romeo, a young man consumed by arithmetic.
Juliet, a lady who counts to one hundred.
Ophelia, a keeper of remainders.

                    Act I: The Counting.

                    Scene I: The Setting Forth.

[Enter Romeo and Juliet]

Juliet:
 You are nothing. Thou art the sum of thyself and a cat!

Romeo:
 You are as lovely as the sum of a fair rose and a lovely lady.

                    Scene II: The Reckoning.

Juliet:
 Thou art the sum of thyself and a cat.
 Am I better than the sum of a big big big big big big cat and a cat?

Romeo:
 If not, let us return to Scene II.

Juliet:
 Open your heart!

Romeo:
 Speak your mind!

[Exeunt]
